Shared message-passing primitives
---------------------------------

Spherical operators in equivariant/ retain the source credits on their
individual implementations. The Jd.pt table in equivariant/data/ is used
by the e3nn 0.4.0 and fairchem eSCN Wigner-D implementation (MIT).
https://github.com/e3nn/e3nn/tree/0.4.0
https://github.com/FAIR-Chem/fairchem

The cgmatrix.npz contraction coefficients in equivariant/data/ are shared
with the So3krates-torch implementation (MIT).
https://github.com/TCPUniLU/So3krates-torch

The shared spherical normalization and gate implementations in nn/ and
equivariant/ follow EquiformerV2 (MIT) and the vendored EquiformerV3
reference. The Cartesian gated blocks in nn/gate.py follow SchNetPack
2.0.4 (MIT).
https://github.com/atomicarchitects/equiformer_v2
https://github.com/atomistic-machine-learning/schnetpack

Nonlocal attention implementations
---------------------------------

nonlocal_/performer.py contains the SpookyNet random-feature attention
implementation. nonlocal_/fragment.py follows the ViSNet-LSRM atom-fragment
attention from LSR-MP. nonlocal_/global_attention.py adapts fairchem
AllScAIP's projected multi-head attention (MIT).
https://github.com/OUnke/SpookyNet
https://github.com/liyy2/LSR-MP
https://github.com/FAIR-Chem/fairchem

Lebedev quadrature data and Euclidean Fast Attention are credited in
nonlocal_/NOTICE.
